# Task 5: File Search using Gemini Online Retrieval Augmented Generation (RAG)

???+ blank "File Search using Gemini"

    ??? info "Introduction"
        
        === "Introduction"
            
            ![CW](./assets/task5a/gem.png)

            Google have introduced a new File Search Tool, a fully managed RAG service built into the Gemini API that can be called with a single API example:https://generativelanguage.googleapis.com/v1beta/fileSearchStores. <a href="https://ai.google.dev/api/file-search/file-search-stores" target="_blank">More info can be found here</a>. 
            
            ![ToolG](./assets/task5a/searTool.png)
            
            In the earlier tasks, we learned how to build our own RAG pipeline using LangChain and vector stores, which gives us a lot of flexibility and control. With Gemini File Search, we now have another option: a managed RAG service where Google handles chunking, indexing, embeddings, and retrieval for us. Instead of replacing the old approach, this simply gives us a choice. For some use cases, building RAG yourself will still make sense for others, using Gemini File Search can reduce complexity so you can focus more on your application and AI-by-design decisions rather than the plumbing.
            
            ![rag6](./assets/task5/rag6.png)
            
            With the File Search Tool, things get much simpler. Instead of managing chunking, embeddings, and retrieval yourself, you just create a file search store and upload your documents. Gemini takes care of splitting, embedding, indexing, and retrieving the right content when you ask a question. This hides the retrieval pipeline so you can focus on your app. File Search gives you an easy, scalable way to ground Gemini on your own data, so answers are more accurate, relevant, and easier to verify. In practice, you simply upload your files, create a store, and let the API handle the rest. A nice bonus is pricing: you only pay for embeddings (depending on the embedding model you use. Default model gemini-embedding-001 at a fixed rate of $0.15 per 1 million tokens ) and for the LLM tokens that are in context. File storage and query-time embeddings are free according to Gemini documentation. For more details on embeddings and pricing, see: <a href="https://ai.google.dev/gemini-api/docs/pricing#gemini-embedding" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">More info on embeddings and pricing</a>. For more details on tokens, see: <a href="https://ai.google.dev/gemini-api/docs/tokens" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">More info on tokens</a>. 
            
            At the time of writing this guide the following models support File Search: gemini-2.5-pro & gemini-2.5-flash. 
            
            See the notes below for the list of supported application and text file types.

